  <title>ECT Delta terminal stapt op 17 augustus over op gezichtsherkenning via de CargoCard</title>
  <link>https://www.ect.nl/nl/nieuws/dossiers/gezichtsherkenning-cargocard/ect-delta-terminal-stapt-op-17-augustus-over-op</link>
  <description>  &lt;div class="layout layout--onecol"&gt;
    &lt;div class="layout__region layout__region--content"&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="field field--name-node-post-date field--type-ds field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;29 July 2026 - 09:42&lt;/div&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Last year, we announced that Hutchison Ports ECT Rotterdam (ECT) would gradually transition to facial recognition as the biometric identification method for truck drivers. The rollout at the ECT Euromax terminal has now been successfully implemented, and we are ready to take the next step in this transition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starting 17 August 2026, the ECT Delta terminal will begin deploying Facial Recognition on Chip (FROC) technology. The implementation will take place in phases, starting with lane 08. ECT aims to transition all six truck lanes at the ECT Delta terminal to facial recognition during 2026, making it the primary biometric identification method for drivers visiting the terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based on the experience gained at the ECT Euromax terminal, the equipment setup at the ECT Delta terminal has been optimized to achieve improved performance and higher recognition success rates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This transition is part of the continued modernization of ECT’s security infrastructure. Facial recognition provides a fast, contactless, and reliable method of identification, supporting our ambition to further enhance both security and operational efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does this mean for CargoCard users?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To maintain access to the ECT Delta terminal, it is essential that drivers have a CargoCard with facial recognition activated. Drivers who have not yet added facial recognition to their CargoCard may eventually be denied access to the terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finger vein technology will remain available during the transition period, but it will ultimately be phased out completely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important next steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If facial recognition has not yet been added to the CargoCard, drivers are advised to update their CargoCard with facial recognition as soon as possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This can be done at Secure Logistics, the issuer of the CargoCard. The Secure Logistics office is located at Hormuzstraat 50, 3199 KW Rotterdam (Maasvlakte), at Maasvlakte Plaza.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Please take into account a transition period during which both biometric systems may operate alongside each other. However, facial recognition will ultimately become the leading identification method.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up-to-date information is available on the ECT website (&lt;a href="http://www.ect.nl"&gt;www.ect.nl&lt;/a&gt;) in the dossier “Facial Recognition at ECT”, including information in multiple languages and answers to frequently asked questions (FAQ).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

</description>
